Purpose: Replace neon lime without making the DS dull or its legends unreadable,
and implement the owner's approved top-edge L/R and square rear rubber pads.

Tasks:
- [x] Use a brighter pale pistachio accent without changing the blue shell/GBA.
- [x] Make face/shoulder lettering and the power symbol dark navy.
- [x] Keep shell-mounted START/SELECT/POWER labels light and readable.
- [x] Give green hinge trim real metallic paint and existing room reflections.
- [x] Keep button/stylus plastic bright without adding scene lights or loops.
- [x] Move L/R from broad underside rectangles to working top-edge buttons.
- [x] Replace four black rectangular feet with matte pale-green square pads.
- [x] Check actual pixels, labels, rear geometry and native shoulder presses.
- [ ] Complete qualification under the bounded CI recovery policy in104.
- [x] Verify actual GitHub issue/Project synchronization and publication.

Acceptance criteria:
Green stays pale but lively. Navy legends remain darker than their button
surfaces under warm and room lighting. Metallic trim remains distinct from
matte rubber pads. Four square pads replace the old black feet; the rear no
longer has large green L/R rectangles. Q/W and native L/R remain functional,
with physical presses into the top edge. Publication is not owner acceptance.

